event: template_sections
data: {"sections":[{"section_id":"header","type":"template","content":"LEGAL NOTICE\n(Under Section 138 read with Section 141 of the Negotiable Instruments Act, 1881)\n\nDate: 04 May 2026\nBy Registered Post A.D. / Speed Post / UPC\n\nTo,\nMr. Vikram Yadav\nPlot 7, Anisabad, Patna - 800002\n\nFrom,\nMr. Ankit Sharma\nThrough: Adv. Rohit Kumar, Advocate\nChamber 15, Civil Court Compound, Patna - 800001","alignment":"left"},{"section_id":"subject_line","type":"template","content":"Subject: Statutory Demand Notice under Section 138 of the Negotiable Instruments Act, 1881 — Cheque No. 458823 dated 25.03.2026 for Rs. 350000/- (Three Lakh Fifty Thousand only) drawn on HDFC Bank, Boring Road Branch, Patna — dishonoured on 04.04.2026\n\nSir/Madam,\n\nUnder instructions from and on behalf of my client, Mr. Ankit Sharma, I hereby serve upon you this statutory notice under Section 138 of the Negotiable Instruments Act, 1881, and call upon you to note as under:","alignment":"left"},{"section_id":"body","type":"ai_generated","content":"1. That my client had advanced a friendly loan of Rs. 3,50,000/- (Rupees Three Lakh Fifty Thousand only) to you on 15.11.2025 for a period of four months. The said loan amount was duly acknowledged in writing by you vide acknowledgment dated 15.11.2025, thereby creating a legally enforceable debt and liability upon you to repay the same to my client.\n\n2. That towards discharge of the aforesaid liability and in settlement of the loan amount, you issued Cheque No. 458823 dated 25.03.2026 for Rs. 3,50,000/- (Rupees Three Lakh Fifty Thousand only) drawn on HDFC Bank, Boring Road Branch, Patna, in favour of my client.\n\n3. That the said cheque was duly presented by my client to the payee's bank on 02.04.2026 for collection and payment. However, the said cheque was returned dishonoured by the drawee bank vide return memo dated 04.04.2026 with the endorsement \"Funds Insufficient\", thereby causing grave financial loss and mental agony to my client.\n\n4. That the dishonour of the aforesaid cheque by you constitutes a criminal offence punishable under Section 138 of the Negotiable Instruments Act, 1881, which provides for imprisonment for a term which may extend to two years, or with fine which may extend to twice the amount of the cheque, or with both.\n\n5. That as per the proviso (b) to Section 138 of the Negotiable Instruments Act, 1881, it is incumbent upon the payee to make a demand for payment of the cheque amount within thirty days of receiving information of the dishonour of the cheque from the bank.\n\n6. That my client received information regarding the dishonour of the said cheque on 04.04.2026, and this notice is being served upon you well within the statutory period of thirty days as mandated under the provisions of Section 138 of the Negotiable Instruments Act, 1881.\n\n7. That the dishonour of the said cheque has not only caused financial hardship to my client but has also damaged the commercial reputation and creditworthiness of my client in the market, thereby entitling my client to claim compensation and damages in addition to the principal cheque amount."},{"section_id":"demand_clause","type":"template","content":"DEMAND\n\nYou are hereby called upon to make payment of the said sum of Rs. 350000/- (Three Lakh Fifty Thousand only) to my client within a period of fifteen (15) days from the date of receipt of this notice, failing which my client shall be constrained to initiate criminal proceedings against you under Section 138 of the Negotiable Instruments Act, 1881, before the competent Magistrate having jurisdiction, at your risk, cost, and consequences.\n\nPlease note that under Section 138, if you fail to make payment within 15 days of receipt of this notice, my client shall file a criminal complaint within 30 days thereafter, and upon conviction you shall be liable to imprisonment for a term which may extend to two years, or with fine which may extend to twice the amount of the cheque, or with both.","alignment":"left"},{"section_id":"closing","type":"template","content":"A copy of this notice is retained in my office for record and further legal action.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\n\n_________________________\nAdv. Rohit Kumar\nAdvocate\nEnrollment No. BCB/3127/2016\nChamber 15, Civil Court Compound, Patna - 800001\n\n(Counsel for Mr. Ankit Sharma)","alignment":"left"},{"section_id":"disclaimer","type":"template","content":"AI-assisted draft — verify with applicable law before filing. Lawie does not provide legal advice.","alignment":"center","style":"footer_small_gray"}]}

